  "officialHtml": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-wr100-900.html",
  "prefLabel": "Env-Wr 402.05 Classification Procedure",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-Wr 402.05 Classification Procedure.\n\n(a) The department shall review all new dam applications to classify the structure in accordance with Env-Wr 101.07.\n\n(b) If the owner disagrees with the department’s hazard classification, the owner shall submit, for review by the department, the following:\n\n(1) The results of a dam breach analysis performed in accordance with Env-Wr 303.02 and Env-Wr 502.04;\n\n(2) Breach routing in accordance with Env-Wr 502.05; and\n\n(3) Inundation mapping in accordance with Env-Wr 503.01.\n\n(c) The owner of a proposed dam shall meet specific requirements relative to design, construction, inspection, and maintenance of the structure in accordance with the applicable provisions of Env-Wr 403.\n\nSource. #8414, eff 8-20-05; ss by #10510, eff 1-22-14; ss by #13980, eff 5-24-24",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-wr100-900.html"
